{
  "name": "sci2code",
  "displayName": "Sci2Code",
  "publisher": "SelfResearchInstitute",
  "author": {
    "name": "The Self Research Institute"
  },
  "repository": {
    "type": "git",
    "url": "https://github.com/The-Self-Research-Institute/Sci2Code-extension-for-vscode"
  },
  "bugs": {
    "url": "https://github.com/The-Self-Research-Institute/Sci2Code-extension-for-vscode/issues",
    "email": "support@selfresearch.org"
  },
  "homepage": "https://github.com/The-Self-Research-Institute/Sci2Code-extension-for-vscode#readme",
  "qna": "https://github.com/The-Self-Research-Institute/Sci2Code-extension-for-vscode/discussions",
  "icon": "resources/Sci2CodeLogo.png",
  "galleryBanner": {
    "color": "#1e1e2e",
    "theme": "dark"
  },
  "description": "Cite from Zotero inside your code and keep your .bib file in sync. Works in Python, R, Julia, JS/TS, Quarto and Typst, including Jupyter notebooks.",
  "license": "MIT",
  "version": "1.0.12",
  "engines": {
    "vscode": "^1.95.0"
  },
  "categories": [
    "Programming Languages",
    "Snippets",
    "Data Science",
    "Education"
  ],
  "keywords": [
    "zotero",
    "citation",
    "reference manager",
    "research",
    "academic",
    "jsdoc",
    "pydoc",
    "bibliography",
    "quarto",
    "typst",
    "scientific",
    "data science",
    "reproducibility",
    "bibtex",
    "jupyter"
  ],
  "activationEvents": [
    "onStartupFinished"
  ],
  "main": "./out/extension.js",
  "contributes": {
    "configuration": {
      "title": "Sci2Code",
      "properties": {
        "sci2code.apiKey": {
          "type": "string",
          "default": "",
          "markdownDescription": "Your Zotero API key with read/write access. Get it from [Zotero API Settings](https://www.zotero.org/settings/keys).\n\n**Security note:** this value is stored locally in your VS Code user settings. It is excluded from Settings Sync, but anyone with access to your machine can read it. The key is also copied into VS Code's secret storage for API calls.",
          "scope": "application",
          "ignoreSync": true,
          "order": 0
        },
        "sci2code.triggers": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "default": [
            "\"\"\"",
            "#",
            "#'",
            "/**"
          ],
          "markdownDescription": "Global comment-trigger strings. When you type any of these above a function, Sci2Code offers a citation completion.\n\nThese triggers apply to **every** language. To add extra triggers for a single language, use `#sci2code.languageSpecificTriggers#` — values there are **merged** with this list, not overridden.\n\nIn **Quarto** and **Typst** text, a trigger that is not a comment marker (for example `&&`) also lists your papers anywhere in the document and cites the one you pick, with no function needed below it. Comment markers such as `#` and `//` keep their usual job.\n\n**What a trigger gives you**: the cursor decides. In code and in Quarto code chunks, a comment trigger above a function inserts a reference comment. In Quarto or Typst text, a custom trigger such as `&&` inserts `@key` and adds the paper to your `.bib`. In Typst, `//` on its own line above a `#let` inserts the reference comment. In Quarto text, `<!--` on its own line does."
        },
        "sci2code.templates": {
          "type": "object",
          "description": "Customize the documentation snippets that are inserted into your code.\n\n**How It Works**:\nThe key is a VS Code Language ID (e.g., `python`) and the value is an array of strings, where each string is a new line.\n\n**Available Placeholders**:\n\n**Common Placeholders**:\n- `${zotero.title}`: The main title of the item.\n- `${zotero.creators}`: A comma-separated list of authors.\n- `${zotero.year}`: The four-digit publication year.\n- `${zotero.date}`: The date exactly as stored in Zotero.\n- `${zotero.DOI}`: The Digital Object Identifier.\n- `${zotero.doiUrl}`: The DOI as a link (https://doi.org/...). Not used by the default templates; the hover popup already shows a clickable DOI link.\n- `${zotero.publicationTitle}`: The title of the journal or book.\n- `${zotero.url}`: The URL link to the item.\n- `${zotero.itemType}`: The type of Zotero item (e.g., 'journalArticle').\n- `${zotero.key}`: The unique Zotero item key.\n\n**Code Context**:\n- `${code.id}`: The unique ID linking the code to the Zotero item.\n- `${code.functionName}`: The name of the function being documented.\n\n**Quarto**: `quarto` is used for comments in the text of a `.qmd`. Inside a code chunk the chunk language's template is used: `python`, `r`, `julia`, and `javascript` for `ojs`.",
          "default": {
            "default": [
              "// Zotero Reference",
              "// Title: ${zotero.title}",
              "// Authors: ${zotero.creators}",
              "// Year: ${zotero.year}",
              "// DOI: ${zotero.DOI}",
              "// URL: ${zotero.url}",
              "// Zotero Key: ${zotero.key}",
              "// Code ID: ${code.id}"
            ],
            "javascript": [
              "/**",
              " * @ZoteroArticleNames ${zotero.title}",
              " * @ZoteroAuthors ${zotero.creators}",
              " * @ZoteroYear ${zotero.year}",
              " * @ZoteroArticleIDs ${zotero.key}",
              " * @ZoteroArticleURLs ${zotero.url}",
              " * @ZoteroDOI ${zotero.DOI}",
              " * @CodeID ${code.id}",
              " */"
            ],
            "typescript": [
              "/**",
              " * @ZoteroArticleNames ${zotero.title}",
              " * @ZoteroAuthors ${zotero.creators}",
              " * @ZoteroYear ${zotero.year}",
              " * @ZoteroArticleIDs ${zotero.key}",
              " * @ZoteroArticleURLs ${zotero.url}",
              " * @ZoteroDOI ${zotero.DOI}",
              " * @CodeID ${code.id}",
              " */"
            ],
            "python": [
              "\"\"\"",
              "Zotero Reference:",
              "    Title: ${zotero.title}",
              "    Authors: ${zotero.creators}",
              "    Year: ${zotero.year}",
              "    DOI: ${zotero.DOI}",
              "    URL: ${zotero.url}",
              "    Key: ${zotero.key}",
              "    CodeID: ${code.id}",
              "\"\"\""
            ],
            "r": [
              "#'",
              "#' @ZoteroArticleIDs: ${zotero.key}",
              "#' @ZoteroItemType: ${zotero.itemType}",
              "#' @ZoteroArticleNames: ${zotero.title}",
              "#' @ZoteroAuthors: ${zotero.creators}",
              "#' @ZoteroYear: ${zotero.year}",
              "#' @ZoteroArticleURLs: ${zotero.url}",
              "#' @ZoteroDOI: ${zotero.DOI}",
              "#' @CodeID: ${code.id}",
              "#'"
            ],
            "julia": [
              "\"\"\"",
              "Reference: ${zotero.title}",
              "Authors: ${zotero.creators}",
              "Year: ${zotero.year}",
              "DOI: ${zotero.DOI}",
              "URL: ${zotero.url}",
              "Zotero Key: ${zotero.key}",
              "Code ID: ${code.id}",
              "\"\"\""
            ],
            "quarto": [
              "<!--",
              "Zotero Reference:",
              "  Title: ${zotero.title}",
              "  Authors: ${zotero.creators}",
              "  Year: ${zotero.year}",
              "  DOI: ${zotero.DOI}",
              "  URL: ${zotero.url}",
              "  Key: ${zotero.key}",
              "  CodeID: ${code.id}",
              "-->"
            ],
            "typst": [
              "/*",
              "Zotero Reference:",
              "  Title: ${zotero.title}",
              "  Authors: ${zotero.creators}",
              "  Year: ${zotero.year}",
              "  DOI: ${zotero.DOI}",
              "  URL: ${zotero.url}",
              "  Key: ${zotero.key}",
              "  CodeID: ${code.id}",
              "*/"
            ]
          }
        },
        "sci2code.languageSpecificTriggers": {
          "type": "object",
          "markdownDescription": "Extra comment triggers scoped to a specific language. Values are **added to** `#sci2code.triggers#` for that language (they do not replace it). The key is a VS Code language id such as `python`, `javascript`, `typescript`, `r`, `julia`, `quarto`, `typst`.\n\nA trigger listed here only works in that language.",
          "default": {
            "javascript": [
              "/**",
              "//"
            ],
            "python": [
              "\"\"\"",
              "#"
            ],
            "julia": [
              "\"\"\"",
              "#"
            ],
            "typescript": [
              "/**",
              "//"
            ],
            "r": [
              "#'",
              "#"
            ],
            "quarto": [
              "<!--",
              "#",
              "#'",
              "\"\"\""
            ],
            "typst": [
              "//",
              "/*"
            ]
          },
          "properties": {
            "javascript": {
              "type": "array",
              "items": {
                "type": "string"
              }
            },
            "typescript": {
              "type": "array",
              "items": {
                "type": "string"
              }
            },
            "python": {
              "type": "array",
              "items": {
                "type": "string"
              }
            },
            "r": {
              "type": "array",
              "items": {
                "type": "string"
              }
            },
            "quarto": {
              "type": "array",
              "items": {
                "type": "string"
              }
            },
            "typst": {
              "type": "array",
              "items": {
                "type": "string"
              }
            },
            "julia": {
              "type": "array",
              "items": {
                "type": "string"
              }
            }
          },
          "additionalProperties": {
            "type": "array",
            "items": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "commands": [
      {
        "command": "sci2code.openSettings",
        "title": "Sci2Code: Open Settings"
      },
      {
        "command": "sci2code.editTemplateForCurrentLanguage",
        "title": "Sci2Code: Edit Citation Template for Current Language"
      },
      {
        "command": "sci2code.resetTemplates",
        "title": "Sci2Code: Reset Citation Templates to Default"
      },
      {
        "command": "sci2code.showLogs",
        "title": "Sci2Code: Show Logs"
      },
      {
        "command": "sci2code.login",
        "title": "Sci2Code: Login to Zotero"
      },
      {
        "command": "sci2code.insertZoteroCitation",
        "title": "Sci2Code: Insert Zotero Citation"
      },
      {
        "command": "sci2code.insertManualCitation",
        "title": "Sci2Code: Insert Manual Citation"
      },
      {
        "command": "sci2code.insertCitationFromSidebar",
        "title": "Sci2Code: Insert Citation From Sidebar"
      },
      {
        "command": "sci2code.generateBibliography",
        "title": "Sci2Code: Generate Bibliography"
      },
      {
        "command": "sci2code.citeInText",
        "title": "Sci2Code: Cite in Text (Quarto and Typst)"
      },
      {
        "command": "sci2code.syncBibliography",
        "title": "Sci2Code: Sync BibTeX File (Append Missing References)"
      },
      {
        "command": "sci2code.logout",
        "title": "Sci2Code: Logout"
      },
      {
        "command": "zotero.refresh",
        "title": "Refresh Library",
        "icon": "$(refresh)"
      },
      {
        "command": "sci2code.openGettingStarted",
        "title": "Sci2Code: Open Getting Started"
      }
    ],
    "menus": {
      "commandPalette": [
        {
          "command": "sci2code.insertCitationFromSidebar",
          "when": "false"
        }
      ]
    },
    "viewsContainers": {
      "activitybar": [
        {
          "id": "zotero-explorer",
          "title": "Zotero",
          "icon": "resources/zotero.svg"
        }
      ]
    },
    "keybindings": [
      {
        "command": "sci2code.insertZoteroCitation",
        "key": "ctrl+alt+c",
        "mac": "cmd+alt+c",
        "when": "editorTextFocus"
      }
    ],
    "views": {
      "zotero-explorer": [
        {
          "type": "webview",
          "id": "sci2code.panel",
          "name": "Sci2Code"
        }
      ]
    },
    "walkthroughs": [
      {
        "id": "sci2code.getStarted",
        "title": "Get started with Sci2Code",
        "description": "Cite papers from your Zotero library in your code and in Quarto and Typst documents.",
        "steps": [
          {
            "id": "connect",
            "title": "Connect your Zotero library",
            "description": "Paste a Zotero API key so Sci2Code can read your library.\n[Connect to Zotero](command:sci2code.login)",
            "media": {
              "markdown": "resources/walkthrough/connect.md"
            },
            "completionEvents": [
              "onCommand:sci2code.login"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "cite-code",
            "title": "Cite a paper in your code",
            "description": "Add a reference above a function in Python, R, Julia, JavaScript or TypeScript.\n[Insert a citation](command:sci2code.insertZoteroCitation)",
            "media": {
              "markdown": "resources/walkthrough/cite-code.md"
            },
            "completionEvents": [
              "onCommand:sci2code.insertZoteroCitation"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "cite-text",
            "title": "Cite a paper in your text (Quarto and Typst)",
            "description": "Put the cursor in a sentence and cite a paper. It is added to your .bib file for you.\n[Cite in Text](command:sci2code.citeInText)",
            "media": {
              "markdown": "resources/walkthrough/cite-text.md"
            },
            "completionEvents": [
              "onCommand:sci2code.citeInText"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "sync",
            "title": "Keep your .bib file in step",
            "description": "Add every paper you cited to the bibliography your document uses.\n[Sync BibTeX File](command:sci2code.syncBibliography)",
            "media": {
              "markdown": "resources/walkthrough/sync.md"
            },
            "completionEvents": [
              "onCommand:sci2code.syncBibliography"
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "scripts": {
    "vscode:prepublish": "npm run compile",
    "compile": "tsc -p ./",
    "watch": "tsc -watch -p ./",
    "pretest": "pnpm run compile && pnpm run lint",
    "lint": "eslint src --ext ts",
    "lint:fix": "eslint src --ext ts --fix",
    "test": "vscode-test",
    "test:unit": "tsc -p ./ && mocha --ui tdd out/test/bibtex.test.js out/test/fixes.test.js out/test/citeFlow.test.js out/test/proseSync.test.js out/test/manifest.test.js out/test/triggerRules.test.js out/test/api.test.js out/test/cache.test.js out/test/delta.test.js out/test/libraryModel.test.js out/test/manualItem.test.js",
    "test-web": "vscode-test-web --browserType=chromium --extensionDevelopmentPath=./",
    "compile-web": "webpack --config webpack.config.js --mode development --watch",
    "package": "vsce package",
    "publish:vsce": "vsce publish",
    "publish:ovsx": "npx --yes ovsx publish"
  },
  "devDependencies": {
    "@types/mocha": "^10.0.9",
    "@types/node": "~20.17.6",
    "@types/vscode": "^1.95.0",
    "@typescript-eslint/eslint-plugin": "^7.18.0",
    "@typescript-eslint/parser": "^7.18.0",
    "@vscode/test-cli": "^0.0.9",
    "@vscode/test-electron": "^2.4.1",
    "@vscode/test-web": "*",
    "assert": "^2.1.0",
    "buffer": "^6.0.3",
    "crypto-browserify": "^3.12.1",
    "eslint": "^8.57.1",
    "https-browserify": "^1.0.0",
    "path-browserify": "^1.0.1",
    "process": "^0.11.10",
    "stream-browserify": "^3.0.0",
    "stream-http": "^3.2.0",
    "ts-loader": "^9.5.2",
    "typescript": "^5.8.3",
    "url": "^0.11.4",
    "util": "^0.12.5",
    "webpack": "^5.99.9",
    "webpack-cli": "^5.1.4"
  }
}